It took me about a year to my first ascension, but by that time I had 
played only nine real games (IIRC).  I had however done four explore 
mode games, two to the ascension and two that I abandoned at a score of 
about a million.  In at least one of them I died about fifty times, in 
the others several tens of times.  So I learned what to avoid (for 
example running around wielding a cockatrice corpse - I fell into a pit, 
but I did not want to die...).  These four games therefore had the value 
of about 100 (or more) real games, each of which would have ended by a 
death.  Nevertheless, I would have had to play more than 100 games to 
gather the same amount of experience, because each early death prevents 
you from seeing the later stages of the game - which does not happen in 
explore mode, so you also learn ways to die later on (being drowned by 
an eel etc.), which is very useful :-).

